  "result": "All 5 tests pass, including the two new ones in `tests/test_t2.py`.\n\n**What changed** in `netgraph/graph.py`, three new methods on `Graph`:\n\n- **`remove_edge(u, v) -> bool`** validates both ids, returns False if the edge is absent, otherwise discards it from both adjacency sets and decrements the edge count. A self-loop is handled correctly since both discards hit the same set.\n- **`degree(u) -> int`** returns the size of the node's neighbour set, so a self-loop contributes exactly one.\n- **`connected_components()`** runs a breadth-first search from each unvisited node in ascending order. Each component is sorted before being appended, and scanning nodes in order guarantees components are ordered by their smallest member. Isolated nodes appear as singleton components.\n\nNo files under `tests/` were touched, and the existing public interface is unchanged.",
